# EVERY QUANTITY A LAYER FILES, AS ROWS RATHER THAN COLUMNS. One row per layer per quantity,
# with the element's own name as the key.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE MODEL ALREADY TREATS THESE AS ONE KIND OF THING AND THE SQL DID NOT.
#    `asrt:Elimination` carries a `quantity` and the corpus files eliminations naming THREE of
#    them -- `demand`, `nameplate` and `draw` -- because two members naming one machine double
#    count the machine as well as the orders. `composition/converted.sqlc` and
#    `composition/fused.sqlc` both answer `'demand' AS quantity` as a literal, so the nameplate
#    and draw eliminations a composer filed and sized are read by nothing.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND A FUSION CAN THEREFORE MOVE A NAMEPLATE IN SILENCE. Demonstrated 2026-09-06 with
#    `examples/witnesses/main.rs`: `merge-group-composition/compute-us` is a ONE-PART fusion with no
#    eliminations, its composed nameplate was moved from 8 GPU to 40 GPU -- five times the
#    single part it is composed from -- and no composition rule noticed.
#
# ⭐ WHY FIVE AND NOT TWO. A layer's demand, its nameplate and its three buffer slacks are all
#   quantities in the layer's own unit that a composition has to carry or account for. The
#   three slacks arrive from `entries/slacks.sqlc` already tall, and the buffer enum names them
#   exactly as the elements do.
#
# ⚠️ AN UNSIZED QUANTITY IS ABSENT FROM THIS RELATION rather than present with a NULL. A row
#    here is a number somebody filed; a caller that needs to know a slack was DECLINED reads
#    entries/slacks.sqlc, where the typed reason lives.
-- pm:Layer's own quantities: demand, nameplate and the three buffer slacks, keyed by element.
SELECT d.filing, d.layer, 'demand' AS quantity,
       d.d_low AS low, d.d_mode AS mode, d.d_high AS high, d.d_unit AS unit
FROM (
    :compose(layers/demand.sqlc)
) d
UNION ALL
SELECT n.filing, n.layer, 'nameplate',
       n.n_low, n.n_mode, n.n_high, n.n_unit
FROM (
    :compose(layers/nameplate.sqlc)
) n
UNION ALL
SELECT s.filing, s.layer, s.buffer || 'Slack',
       s.low, s.mode, s.high, s.unit
FROM (
    :compose(entries/slacks.sqlc)
) s
WHERE s.low IS NOT NULL
